course: dictionary
lesson: 3467
title: Magic words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your head, and fairyland is one of them. The author uses «faery», an old spelling of fairyland, in «a gleaming carpet of faery». The word gleaming tells you the wood sparkled like a magical place.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The powder is fine, it caresses the cheek and it makes a tingle. These words are soft, bright and magical, so faery must mean something beautiful and unreal, not an ordinary wood. Then test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: You can find fairyland in everyday life too. «The garden looks like fairyland with all its lights» describes a place that seems too beautiful to be real. The author is comparing the garden to a magical land, so you can understand the picture without a fairy story.
fact: Fairyland means the magical, imaginary land where fairies live in stories.
fact: Fairyland also means a place so beautiful, sparkling or magical that it seems unreal.
fact: «Faery» is an old spelling that means fairyland.
fact: «Delicate» means light, fine and easily damaged, so the snowy wood looked too delicate to be walked on.
fact: Alice in Wonderland is not called fairyland, but it is a magical dream-land of the same kind.
exercise: The snow made the wood «a gleaming carpet of faery». What does faery mean here? | *Fairyland | A cold, empty field | A kind of snowball | A dark cave
exercise: «The garden looked like fairyland with all its lights.» What does the sentence tell you about the garden? | It was a place for doing sums | *It was beautiful and magical, as if unreal | It was full of rough, heavy stones | It was dark, dirty and empty
exercise: Find and copy one word from «caressed the cheek with a tingle» that means touched gently. | *caressed | tingle | with | cheek
test: Which is true about fairyland in stories? | It is a school playground | It is a sweet shop | It is a type of car | *It is the magical land where fairies live
test: Why might an author write «like fairyland» about a snowy forest? | To show it is very cold and dull | To show the forest is for fairies to clean | *To show it is so beautiful and sparkling that it seems magical | To show it has no trees at all
exam: Which clue best shows the wood is more than an ordinary wood? | *The word gleaming, which shows it sparkles like something magical | The word feet, which is a body part | The word wood, which is a plain word | The word the, which is very common
